          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly and emphatically avows the narrator's present love for Maria. It answers her question about whether his apparent change is genuine rather than something temporary that he will regret.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"The focal avowal has substantial undertaking force because it is governed by the oath-like asseveration “Saavist … saavist” and is immediately restated as love applying in pleasure and distress, ordinary days and celebrations. Thus this occurrence affirms an enduring relational bond, rather than merely reporting a passing feeling. The shared-life statement further clarifies that commitment. Although that statement is grammatically distinct, it belongs to the same answer and elaborates the force of the focal avowal rather than supplying an unrelated promise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"Despite the highly emotional reunion, the focal expression is presented as a considered answer to Maria's request for assurance, not as a reflex-like cry or affective discharge. Its emotional delivery does not displace its avowing and undertaking functions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.89,\"reason\":\"The expression also reassures Maria, but that pragmatic effect is adequately explained by its emphatic avowal and affirmation of enduring commitment. No distinct residual core force is established.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotionally intense reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent commitment is real, lasting, and not merely a consequence of temporarily missing his lover. He responds directly with the focal declaration and then elaborates it as love enduring across hardship and ordinary life, oriented toward a long shared future.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The narrator affirms that he is bound to love Maria across pleasure and hardship and envisages living with her for a long time. The terms remain broad rather than formally specified. Maria's tears, happiness, and narrated understanding that he speaks truly establish positive emotional uptake, though no separate formal acceptance is stated.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence is narrated from the speaker's own perspective and strongly presents his declaration as truthful, but it does not independently verify sincerity, define the relationship's formal status, or establish eventual fulfilment beyond this scene.\"}"
